{"kind":"artifact","text":"internal/app implementation at exact clean pushed head f02ea9b142bd8f78f733b6487cd4c063b456b6c9.\n\nTHE BRIEF WAS WRONG AND THE WORK CORRECTED IT. I asked for the View accessor to be fixed; there was none. apphost.Config escaped through the exported Workspace.Config field, read directly by every consumer, so there was no boundary to harden. View() at app.go:460 is now that boundary and returns Config.Clone(). Every external production reader is converted; I grepped and none remain.\n\nRESIDUAL GAP, STATED NOT BURIED. The field stays exported because four test files across cmd/gitseq-github, cmd/gitseq-mcp, cmd/gs and internal/app seed or inspect it as fixtures. Its doc comment records that contract, but the compiler does not prevent future external production code from reading the field directly. That is the honest limit of this design.\n\nAttachConfig at app.go:469 creates via CreateConfig, tolerates os.ErrExist from a race loser, and routes every path including the creating one through Open plus the ReadOnly, genesis and format comparison -- so a success means the STORED genesis, not an echo of the argument.\n\nTestConcurrentAttachAndOpenAgreeOnStoredGenesis pins the interleaving with an explicit gate rather than hoping for a race. Its first version was a stochastic eight-way race that PASSED 5 of 5 against the broken code, because subprocess jitter serialised the entrants; it was dropped rather than shipped. Against the unfixed code the pinned version fails deterministically with 'reported success, but the store finally holds ...: its update was lost'. I reproduced that myself by deleting the post-open genesis comparison.\n\nNOT DONE, and outside the conditions: no internal locking was added, so a resident mutating custody while serving concurrent View calls can still race internally; and the SaveConfig stale-whole-file lost update is untouched. gofmt clean over every tracked Go file plus both new test files, go vet ./... clean, go test -count=1 ./... pass across 28 packages, race on internal/app 62.492s internal/apphost and internal/service 21.655s, internal/docset pass in 46.165s, GOOS=windows GOARCH=amd64 go build ./... clean, git diff --check clean, worktree clean, origin equals the head. I re-ran gofmt, vet, the Windows build and the full suite myself, and independently reproduced two of the mutations.","body":{"commit":"f02ea9b142bd8f78f733b6487cd4c063b456b6c9","path":"internal/app"}}